[{"slug": "washington-squatters-rights-adverse-possession", "title": "Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: What Owners Should Know", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: What Owners Should Know</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Washington</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession sale</li><li>Turn the Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Washington House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Washington law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Actions to recover real property or its possession must be brought within ten years; plaintiff must show seisin or possession within ten years before the action. (RCW 4.16.020(1); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=4.16.020' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Adverse possession under claim and color of title: actual, open and notorious possession under claim and color of title made in good faith, for seven successive years, plus payment of all taxes legally assessed during that time, makes the possessor legal owner to the extent of the paper title. (RCW 7.28.070; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=7.28.070' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Actual, open and notorious possession for seven successive years with a connected title in law or equity deducible of record: owner&#x27;s recovery action must be brought within seven years after possession taken. (RCW 7.28.050; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=7.28.050' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Criminal trespass in the first degree: knowingly entering or remaining unlawfully in a building; a gross misdemeanor. (RCW 9A.52.070; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=9A.52.070' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>In an unlawful detainer action the plaintiff may apply for a writ of restitution restoring the property; the writ is issued by the superior court clerk and is returnable in twenty days; a bond is required if issued before judgment. (RCW 59.12.090; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.090' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Washington?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Washington houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Washington house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Washington attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-eviction-notice/'>Washington Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Washington guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/'>We buy houses in Washington</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=4.16.020' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 4.16.020(1)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=7.28.070' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 7.28.070</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=7.28.050' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 7.28.050</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=9A.52.070' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 9A.52.070</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.090' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.12.090</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Washington house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Washington attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Washington\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Washington squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "washington squatters rights"}, {"slug": "washington-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Washington</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Washington House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Washington statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Landlord must give a full and specific statement of the basis for retaining any deposit, with any refund, within 30 days after the tenancy ends and the premises are vacated (or 30 days after learning of abandonment); failure makes landlord liable for the full deposit. (RCW 59.18.280(1)(a), (2); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.280' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Deposits must be placed promptly in a trust account at a Washington financial institution or licensed escrow agent; tenant gets written receipt and notice of depository; on transfer of landlord status the deposit is transferred to the successor landlord. (RCW 59.18.270; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.270' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Tenant ends a month-to-month tenancy by written notice of 20 days or more before the end of the period (this section governs the tenant&#x27;s notice). (RCW 59.18.200(1)(a); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.200' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord must give at least two days&#x27; written notice of intent to enter (except emergency or impracticable), at reasonable times; one day&#x27;s notice suffices to show the unit to prospective or actual purchasers or tenants. (RCW 59.18.150(6); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.150' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Rent increases require a minimum of 90 days&#x27; prior written notice (30 days for income-based subsidized tenancies) and cannot take effect before the end of the rental agreement term. (RCW 59.18.140(3); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.140' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord must keep premises fit for human habitation, substantially comply with codes affecting health or safety, and maintain structural components (roofs, floors, walls, foundations) in reasonably good repair. (RCW 59.18.060(1)-(2); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may not take or threaten reprisals or retaliatory action against a tenant in compliance with the chapter because of good faith and lawful exercises of listed tenant rights. (RCW 59.18.240; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.240' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Washington?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Washington houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-eviction-notice/'>Washington Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Washington guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/'>We buy houses in Washington</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.280' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.280(1)(a), (2)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.270' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.270</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.200' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.200(1)(a)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.150' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.150(6)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.140' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.140(3)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.060(1)-(2)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.240' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.240</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Washington\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights", "rank_math_description": "Washington landlord tenant law and tenant rights: deposits, notices, entry and selling a rented house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "washington tenant rights"}, {"slug": "washington-eviction-notice", "title": "Washington Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Washington Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Washington</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Washington Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Washington Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Washington Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Washington House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Washington law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Nonpayment of rent: written notice to pay or vacate; 14 days after service for tenancies under chapter 59.18 RCW (3 days for others). (RCW 59.12.030(3); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.030' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Lease violation (other than rent): written notice to perform or vacate, 10 days after service. (RCW 59.12.030(4); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.030' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A landlord may not evict, refuse to continue a tenancy, or end a periodic tenancy except for enumerated causes (just cause); no-cause termination is not allowed. (Page version is the one effective Jan 1, 2028.). (RCW 59.18.650(1)(a); <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.650' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Eviction is an unlawful detainer action in superior court; the writ of restitution is issued by the superior court clerk. (RCW 59.12.090; <a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.090' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Washington?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Washington houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Washington Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Washington Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Washington guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/'>We buy houses in Washington</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.030' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.12.030(3)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.18.650' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.18.650(1)(a)</a></li><li><a href='https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=59.12.090' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RCW 59.12.090</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Washington Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Washington\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-washington/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Washington Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/washington-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Washington Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Washington eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "washington eviction notice"}]